                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e326ccb-016c-3b19-8935-e5038de28596",
                        "entry_id": "f82c76f3-b563-340a-9874-90adf180d9d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the action or habit (by a lawyer or, figuratively, anyone) of making pedantic, petty, sophistical, or contemptible arguments or legal maneuvers; pettifogging; rules lawyering"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab3d6d73-879e-30fe-95e5-1faf5a387f12",
                        "entry_id": "f82c76f3-b563-340a-9874-90adf180d9d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "such an argument"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f9c2b54-2f05-4907-a578-7acaa4b28d85",
                                "sense_id": "ab3d6d73-879e-30fe-95e5-1faf5a387f12",
                                "text": "Le Tribunal ajoute que le fait de ne pas procéder par requête en vertu de la Charte et d’invoquer en plaidoirie que l’une des conditions d’application de la présomption d’identité n’a pas été prouvée hors de tout doute raisonnable ne constitue pas une embuscade ni une avocasserie. Il s’agit simplement de l’application des principes fondamentaux relatifs au droit au silence, à la présomption d’innocence et à la nécessité d’une preuve hors de tout doute raisonnable.",
                                "translation": "The Court adds that proceeding not by a Charter application, but instead by pleading that one of the conditions for applying the presumption of identity has not been proven beyond a reasonable doubt, constitutes neither an ambush nor a tricky legal maneuver. It is simply the application of the fundamental principles relating to the right to silence, the presumption of innocence, and the need for proof beyond a reasonable doubt.",
                                "english": "The Court adds that proceeding not by a Charter application, but instead by pleading that one of the conditions for applying the presumption of identity has not been proven beyond a reasonable doubt, constitutes neither an ambush nor a tricky legal maneuver. It is simply the application of the fundamental principles relating to the right to silence, the presumption of innocence, and the need for proof beyond a reasonable doubt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "785680b7-22a3-46d3-8f5a-692aaa4d475a",
                                "sense_id": "ab3d6d73-879e-30fe-95e5-1faf5a387f12",
                                "text": "...se magasiner une cape d’invisibilité juridique en invoquant le no-fault, c’est une avocasserie qui serait risible si on ne parlait pas de la mort d’un enfant de 5 ans.",
                                "translation": "Trying to buy a legal invisibility cloak by invoking no-fault insurance is a contemptible legal maneuver that would be laughable if we were not talking about the death of a 5-year-old child.",
                                "english": "Trying to buy a legal invisibility cloak by invoking no-fault insurance is a contemptible legal maneuver that would be laughable if we were not talking about the death of a 5-year-old child."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
